{{also|Thalamus}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|thalamus|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|θάλαμος||an inner chamber, a bedroom, a bed|tr=thalamos|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
{{en-noun|thalami|pl2=thalamuses}}

# {{anatomy}} Either of two large, ovoid structures of grey matter within the [[forebrain]] that relay sensory impulses to the [[cerebral cortex]].
# {{botany}} The [[receptacle]] of a [[flower]]; a [[torus]].
# A [[thallus]].

